@codelaw/rules-data / codelaw-rules-data

This pack ships no third-party data tables.

The Markdown rules are reimplementations written for codelaw. Their
`ported_from:` fields name the markdownlint rules (version 0.42.0,
https://github.com/DavidAnson/markdownlint — Copyright (c) David Anson,
released under the MIT License) whose documented behaviour they reproduce; no
markdownlint code or documentation text is included.

The ordering convention of `json/package-scripts-sorted` follows
sort-package-json (https://github.com/keithamus/sort-package-json, MIT License);
no code from it is included.

The JSON, YAML and TOML rules are written from the format specifications
(RFC 8259, YAML 1.2.2, YAML 1.1, TOML 1.0.0) and the Python packaging
specifications (PEP 503, PEP 621). No code, text or rule definitions are taken
from yamllint (GPL-3.0).
